I committed the #993 fix as 4c6fb486, but the end-to-end test the task asked for is missing. I never ran the -p + Ctrl+C scenario either before or after the change, so the new behaviour is untested in a real run. Build, cargo test, clippy with -D warnings, and cargo fmt --check all pass.

What changed
• **Exit code: a `-p` or piped-stdin run cut short by Ctrl+C now exits 130** instead of 0, so a script can tell a partial answer from a complete one.
• **The note: it now says `(interrupted)` and goes to stderr**. The old "press Ctrl+C again to exit" hint no longer lands at the end of the answer on stdout. Any text already streamed stays on stdout.
• **No follow-up work after an interrupt:** in piped mode, the auto-continue loop no longer starts a new turn.
• REPL: unchanged. It still prints the same hint to the same place.
• **JSON mode** (`--output-format json`) also exits 130 on interrupt because it shares the same exit-code path. The JSON output itself is produced the same way as before. Stream-JSON has its own Ctrl+C handling and was not touched.
• I added a line to `CHANGELOG.md under [Unreleased], and the commit message says this shipped after v0.2.0. I didn't check whether docs/src/usage/single-prompt.md` documents exit codes, so that page may still need a 130 line.

The new code is in src/prompt/interrupt.rs rather than src/prompt.rs. prompt.rs was already over its recorded size, and adding the code there tripped the size-limit test. I moved it rather than raise the limit.

Not done
• **No end-to-end test and no positive control.** I ran out of budget before writing the test that sends SIGINT to a real `yoyo -p` against a stalled stub server. The only test is a small table test on the note text, which checks that the REPL hint is unchanged byte for byte and that the -p note doesn't say "again". Nothing tests the stderr routing, the exit code 130, or what stdout contains.
• **Possible lost partial line (I noticed this but did not check it):** the interrupt path doesn't flush the markdown renderer's buffer, so text still waiting in it may never reach stdout. This was already true before my change.

The commit message records both gaps. Next step: write the SIGINT test in tests/print_stdout_contract.rs, waiting for the first streamed bytes before sending the signal, then run the positive control.

